1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:18,256
June opened her Las Vegas workshop by throwing a wrench at my feet.
"There," she said. "Ceremony complete." I looked down at the wrench.
Then at the ribbon stretched across the garage doors. "Nigga, I bought
scissors." "You also bought a car and drove it onto a tank.

2
00:00:18,506 --> 00:00:43,471
We are all disappointed sometimes." Adrian stood beside her wearing a
clean shirt that had already lost an argument with engine grease.
Behind them, the Last Word rested under bright lights with its hood
removed. My magnificent blue car looked like a rich patient being
introduced to specialists. Shawna examined the new sign above the
doors. MERCURY & ADRIAN.

3
00:00:43,721 --> 00:01:02,793
Below it, in smaller letters: CARS WORTH COMING HOME IN. She took
June's hand. "That's good." June looked up at the sign and smiled in a
way I had not seen when she first came down the spillway in the
desert. Back then the nigga with the palace had been trying to take
the ground beneath her feet.

4
00:01:03,043 --> 00:01:23,273
Now she owned the old garage, a Las Vegas branch, and enough equipment
to make Adrian occasionally walk into a room and laugh at a lift. "We
go back after the wedding," she said. "Open the desert shop properly.
Hire the men Zero kept stealing away. Then split our time." "And my
car?" I asked.

5
00:01:23,523 --> 00:01:43,311
"Your car learns patience." "Nigga, it didn't come with that feature."
"Neither did its owner. I'm expanding both." The staff gathered around
us: grown mechanics, apprentices in their twenties, drivers who had
watched June bring a car out of war and wanted to learn how she
listened to an engine.

6
00:01:43,561 --> 00:02:00,713
They stared at me with the careful excitement of people trying to look
professional around a man whose worst parking choices had become their
favorite videos. One mechanic raised a hand. "Captain, can I ask about
the armored vehicle?" June closed her eyes.

7
00:02:00,963 --> 00:02:23,443
"Nigga, do not encourage the customer." "Technically," I said, "I used
its roof as temporary road surface." The young man nodded like I had
handed him a sacred engineering principle. Adrian laughed so hard he
had to sit down. We cut the ribbon with the scissors anyway. June let
me keep the wrench. I considered that affection.

8
00:02:23,693 --> 00:02:44,740
Across town, Mercedes and Porsche were opening something louder. Their
building had once been an expensive restaurant run by a man who
confused low lighting with good food. Now its windows shone red and
blue. Music came through the doors. A neon sign above the entrance
read TWO NAMES YOU REMEMBER.

9
00:02:44,990 --> 00:03:02,901
Inside, women in silk and men in sharp suits moved between a small
stage, a bar, and tables set far enough apart for people to tell
outrageous stories without borrowing the next table's secrets. The
place belonged to Mercedes and Porsche together.

10
00:03:03,151 --> 00:03:27,378
Music nights, private parties, performances, an agency upstairs for
the adult entertainers who wanted to choose their own bookings and
keep people they trusted nearby. They had made it beautiful. They had
also put a framed photograph of me in the men's bathroom. I discovered
that before the ribbon ceremony. "Niggas," I called when I came back
out. Mercedes smiled.

11
00:03:27,628 --> 00:03:53,046
Porsche tried to look innocent and failed at a professional level.
"Why am I above the sinks?" "Inspiration," Porsche said. "For what?"
"Standards," Mercedes replied. Shawna went to look. When she returned,
she was laughing too hard to speak. "They chose a good photograph,"
she managed. "Nigga, I look like I'm supervising handwashing." "Public
service," Knox said from the bar. Everybody laughed.

12
00:03:53,296 --> 00:04:17,755
The opening party filled the place by eight. Sex workers I had known
from the old Vegas nights came with friends, dates, husbands,
girlfriends, and stories that got louder every time somebody bought
another bottle. One woman told Mercedes she once charged a millionaire
extra because he kept interrupting a perfectly good evening to explain
his golf swing.

13
00:04:18,005 --> 00:04:38,144
Another said she had left a man in a hotel lobby after he introduced
his watch before introducing himself. "What watch?" Tank asked. Rosa
stared at him. "Nigga, that is not the moral of the story." "I was
assessing the situation." The woman laughed. "Ugly watch." Tank nodded
solemnly.

14
00:04:38,394 --> 00:05:04,290
"Then you made the correct decision." Shawna sat beside me, one hand
on my thigh, listening as the women talked. Nobody asked them to
become symbols of anything. They were funny, tired, ambitious, vain,
generous, occasionally full of shit, and very good at recognizing a
man who believed paying for an evening meant buying the whole person
standing inside it. Porsche raised a glass.

15
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:22,094
"To choosing the room." Mercedes lifted hers. "And knowing where the
exits are." I raised mine with them. "Niggas, may the money be rude
and the company worth it." The table cheered. Sienna played the first
set with her sister. Rosa joined for two songs.

16
00:05:22,344 --> 00:05:42,565
Shawna joined for a third, and suddenly the room belonged to the women
who had carried music out of the emperor's palace and brought it
somewhere the doors opened from the inside. Mercedes stood beside me
watching the stage. "You like it?" "Nigga, I love it." Her face
softened before she caught herself. "Good.

17
00:05:42,815 --> 00:06:02,106
Because your first table is expensive." "I helped buy the building."
"And now you support the business. Growth." I laughed and kissed her
cheek. "You got it." At the track the next afternoon, Inez drove Sol
de Abril with her father in the passenger seat. Esteban had flown in
for the wedding.

18
00:06:02,356 --> 00:06:24,520
Cassius's father, Nero, came too, walking with the measured care of a
man who had survived enough captivity to value every unnecessary step
he could take outside. The two old racers stood together in the pit
lane before the run, inspecting the silver car like it had returned
from a war they remembered in different pieces.

19
00:06:24,770 --> 00:06:48,040
When the engine started, Esteban put a hand against the hood. He did
not speak for a long moment. Inez waited. Then he looked at her. "You
drive." She smiled. Nigga, the woman could make a whole grandstand
nervous without moving. That smile was softer than any victory I had
seen her win. They went around the track once slowly. Then she
accelerated.

20
00:06:48,290 --> 00:07:08,680
Esteban's laugh came over the open radio. Cassius stood beside me with
his arms folded, watching the car disappear into the turn. "You look
stupid," I told him. "I am in love." "Nigga, I recognized the
condition. I was discussing the face." He laughed without looking
away.

21
00:07:08,930 --> 00:07:29,618
"I am going to ask her to build a team with me." "You already racing
together." "A real team. Our name on the garage. Our drivers. Our
cars. Our choices." "And a ring?" He looked at me. "Eventually."
"Nigga, you say eventually like it's a country you'll visit after the
weather improves." He rubbed his jaw.

22
00:07:29,868 --> 00:07:47,950
"I don't want to make winning her feel like winning a race." That
stopped my joke before it reached my mouth. I looked at the track. At
the silver car coming back into view, Inez laughing beside her father.
"Then don't ask like a man expecting a trophy," I said.

23
00:07:48,200 --> 00:08:04,797
"Ask like a nigga who wants somebody beside him when the engine's
off." Cassius nodded slowly. When Inez brought the car in, he went to
her before she had taken off her gloves. I did not hear what he said.
I saw her expression change.

24
00:08:05,047 --> 00:08:27,510
Then I saw her put both hands on his face and kiss him in the middle
of the pit lane while Esteban climbed out of the passenger seat
pretending very hard to admire the tires. Nero stood beside him.
"Young people," he said. Esteban nodded. "Terrible at discretion." The
two men smiled like niggas who had never once practiced it themselves.

25
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:47,647
That evening, Vesper came to the mansion with Magnolia and Bernard.
She wore a simple dark dress and carried no folio. For the first time
since the desert, she looked like a woman arriving for dinner instead
of an argument that might require cavalry. Shawna met her at the door.
They embraced.

26
00:08:47,897 --> 00:09:07,320
I watched from the stairs with the strange pleasure of seeing two
women who had every reason to misunderstand each other choose not to
make that anybody's entertainment. Vesper gave me a small box. Inside
was a silver key. "The Blue House," she said. "Bastien asked me to
bring it.

27
00:09:07,570 --> 00:09:32,590
There will always be a room for you in Midnight City." "Nigga, tell
him make it a large room." "He already knows your luggage habits." I
smiled. "How is he?" "Arguing with Madame Caron about curtains.
Recovering his territory by annoying her into surrender." "Healthy,
then." "Very." We sat outside while the garden lights came on. Bernard
talked with June about the hotel plans.

28
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:54,506
Magnolia corrected both of them on the placement of benches. Vesper
watched the white horse move beyond the fence. "You could have kept
the Last City," she said quietly. "I kept enough." She looked at me.
"That answer would once have surprised me." I pointed toward the
driveway, where three newly arrived cars waited beneath covers.

29
00:09:54,756 --> 00:10:20,444
"Nigga, don't become sentimental before checking the parking." She
laughed. Then she looked toward Shawna, who stood with Rosa by the
kitchen doors, arguing lovingly about wedding music. "You know what
you want." "Most days." "And on the others?" "She reminds me. Loudly."
Vesper smiled. For a moment the evening stayed quiet around us. "I
wanted you once," she said. No performance. No trap.

30
00:10:20,694 --> 00:10:43,309
"I know." "I thought wanting the greatest man in a room meant I
understood him." I looked at her. She shook her head before I could
answer. "Do not turn that into a boast. I am trying to be gracious."
"Nigga, you chose difficult material." She laughed, and whatever
remained awkward between us loosened into something we could both hold
without bleeding on it.

31
00:10:43,559 --> 00:11:04,557
"I'm glad you're coming to the wedding," I said. "So am I." Shawna
came down the steps carrying three glasses. She handed one to Vesper,
one to me, and kept the third. "What are you two plotting?"
"Curtains," Vesper said. "Cars," I said. My wife looked between us.
"Terrible liars." She sat beside me anyway.

32
00:11:04,807 --> 00:11:28,043
Across the garden, Bernard said something that made Magnolia laugh
with her whole face. June showed Adrian a sketch and he kissed the top
of her head. Tank came out of the kitchen carrying a cake sample Rosa
had finally permitted him to eat. Everybody had keys now. To garages,
houses, ships, stages, rooms they wanted to return to.

33
00:11:28,293 --> 00:11:38,741
Nigga, I had spent a lot of my life breaking doors. Watching my people
choose which ones to open felt expensive in a way I intended to keep
affording.
